VU1 helper de-duplication: the exactness helpers are shared by the generated blocks

This patch used to carry the change that removes the duplicated copies of the
VU1 exactness helpers (the operand normalisation, the MAC/clip flag helpers
and the clamp helpers), so that the exact build, the fast build (patch 51) and
the x86-64 JIT (patch 18) call one set of helpers instead of one copy per
build.

Its content is in the chain already: the helpers live in
PS2Recomp/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/vu/ps2_vu1_native.inl and in
PS2Recomp/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_vu1_native.h, and the patches that
carry them are 51-vu1-fast-mode.patch (the vu1n::fast variants of the
exactness helpers) and 18-vu1-x64-jit.patch (the JIT's calls into them).
Rebuilding the stack against the working tree (tools/pipeline/rebuild_patch_stack.py)
found nothing left to say here: the files this patch touches are already in
their working-tree state at this point of the chain, so this file is kept as
the place where that change is documented and it carries no file diff of its
own. The pipeline applies it with --allow-empty.

The helpers are shared through the single namespace of vu1n (the exactness
helpers in ps2_vu1_native.h, the fast variants in ps2_vu1_native.inl), so a
helper is defined once and both builds call it; the x86-64 JIT calls them
through the same HelperFn table (ps2_vu1_x64.inl).
